# A clang sanitizer special-case list for OpenSSL's ASan+UBSan flavour (build_deps.sh asan). It
# is passed only to OpenSSL's Configure, so "src:*" below means every source file of OpenSSL and
# nothing else.
#
# OpenSSL calls typed functions through generic function-pointer types by design, in macros of
# its public headers: DEFINE_STACK_OF (safestack.h) casts each typed free, compare and copy
# function to OPENSSL_sk_freefunc, OPENSSL_sk_compfunc and OPENSSL_sk_copyfunc; IMPLEMENT_PEM_read
# (pem.h) casts d2i_X509 and its kin to d2i_of_void; DEFINE_LHASH_OF does the same for hash,
# compare and doall callbacks. clang 22's -fsanitize=function, part of -fsanitize=undefined for
# C, reports each such call. M2a's development checks on L met two of them, one per run, since
# UBSan stops at the first report:
#   crypto/stack/stack.c line 440, OPENSSL_sk_pop_free calling pd_free(OSSL_PROPERTY_DEFINITION *)
#     through OPENSSL_sk_freefunc (from crypto/property/property_parse.c line 400);
#   crypto/pem/pem_oth.c line 31, PEM_ASN1_read_bio calling d2i_X509 through d2i_of_void (from
#     PEM_read_bio_X509).
# The sites are as many as the uses of those macros, so the function check is left out of all of
# OpenSSL. Every other UBSan check stays on in all of OpenSSL; oneport's own code and nghttp2 keep
# the function check. Declared in bench/coverage.json.
[function]
src:*
